==Usage== <!--T:6-->

<!--T:7-->
# Select a [[Image:Silk_ControlPoly6.svg|16px]] [[Silk_ControlPoly6|6 point control polygon]] in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]] or in the [[3D_View|3D View]].
# There are several ways to invoke the command.
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|16px]] CubicCurve_6}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Silk → [[Image:Silk_CubicCurve_6.svg|16px]] CubicCurve_6}} option from the menu.
# A cubic curve, a '''CubicCurve_6''' object, is created.

==Notes== <!--T:19-->

<!--T:20-->
* A 6-control-point cubic NURBS curve. G2 continuous throughout; G3 continuous throughout except at two points along the curve, where it is G2 only.
* The practical use of this curve is to preview blends on curves before doing the full work of blending surfaces.
* This is currently an endpoint in the Silk design workflow.
* The input ControlPoly6 can be used to build grids and surfaces; alternatively, this curve can be used with the rest of FreeCAD — extruded, revolved, etc. — if curve design is all that is needed from Silk.

== Properties == <!--T:8-->

<!--T:9-->
See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

<!--T:10-->
A '''CubicCurve_6''' object is derived from a [[[Part_Feature|Part feature]], or more precise a {{Incode|Part::FeaturePython}} object, and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:

=== Data === <!--T:11-->

<!--T:12-->
{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

<!--T:13-->
* {{PropertyData|Poly|Link}}: Control polygon.
* {{PropertyData|reverse|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the parameter direction.

<!--T:14-->
{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

<!--T:15-->
* {{PropertyData|internalName|String}}: The permanent internal FreeCAD name for this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|CubicCurve_6}}. The workbench class used to create this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_version|String}}: The class version of this object.


